KZ3 4004: a title's own DNS client answered locally from the name map. KZ3's Medius rt_socket resolves the MUIS host
itself: it reads the primary DNS from cellNetCtl (GetInfo code 19) and sends a UDP query to port 53 (seen in a Proton
run, network pass 4: "refused UDP 8.8.8.8:53", login stuck on "Connecting.."). In strict mode a UDP datagram to port 53
(sendto, or send on a socket connect()ed to port 53) never reaches the host: net_policy parses the question (bounded:
one question, plain labels, <= 512 bytes) and builds the reply (mapped name: one A record with the server's address;
anything else: NXDOMAIN); the next recv/recvfrom on that socket returns it from the queried address, and poll/select
report the socket readable. Also in strict mode, a UDP datagram to a refused destination is dropped and reported as
sent (logged once) instead of failing with EHOSTUNREACH: KZ3's NAT code sends a UPnP search to 239.255.255.250:1900,
and a send error there may end the login (ASSUMPTION; a lost datagram is normal UDP). Outside strict mode nothing
changes. Test: tools/net/test_net.sh (test_kz3_net part 7).

